  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Hair Match** (1 review): Opening with this song let the attendee see the singer under bright stage light, a lasting memory [4]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **I'd Really Love to See You Tonight (John Ford Coley)**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Shirtless in Hamburg**: rare: 10 archived performances [5]\n- **Keeping House**: rare: 5 archived performances [5]\n- **Bleed Out**: back after 57 archived shows (500 days); rare: 3 archived performances [5]\n- **I Hope You Dance (Lee Ann Womack)**: rare: 4 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2024-01-31.MATRIX** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 21 songs; 84 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer likes the tone and detail captured by the microphones used on this matrix recording [3]\n- **tMG2024-01-31**: matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 19 songs; 84 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage banter reminded the listener of Dave King going off on tangents [3]\n- Attendee sat in the ADA section, which they also used for professional wrestling events at the Rialto [4]\n- Recorded from the Rialto balcony; Brandon Eggleston ran the board on this tour [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2024-01-31.MATRIX**: taped by Aaron Miller; transferred by Aaron Miller; source: Microtech Gefell M300 > Zoom F3 + SBD > Sony PCM-A10 [1]. Also: Matrix mixes Microtech Gefell M300 mics through a Zoom F3 with a soundboard feed recorded on a Sony PCM-A10; Transfer used iZotope RX 7 then xAct to FLAC at 24 bit, 48 kHz [1]\n- **tMG2024-01-31**: taped by @LMGBTapes on tweeter; transferred by @LMGBTapes on tweeter; source: SBD > Sony PCM-A10 + Neumann KM184s (FOB) > Tascam DR-680mkii + CA-14 Omnis (Healy On Stage) > CA-Ugly 2 > Sony PCM-A10 [2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by KXCI: [KXCI Presents! The Mountain Goats, Craig Finn and Bully Giveaway Contest, KXCI](https://kxci.org/2024/01/kxci-presents-the-mountain-goats-craig-finn-and-bully-giveaway-contest/) [6]",
